      "titulo": {
        "en": "The natural world"
      },
      "texto": {
        "en": "Animals are **domésticos** or **salvajes**. They are **mamíferos**, **aves**, **reptiles**, **peces** or **insectos**. They live in **la selva**, **el bosque**, **el desierto**, **el mar**.\n\n**El ave** is feminine. It takes **el** only because it begins with a stressed a: **el** ave **pequeña**, **las** aves. The same happens with **el agua** and **el águila**.\n\nA plant has **raíces**, **un tronco** (if it is a tree), **ramas**, **hojas** and **flores**. You **plantas** it, **riegas** it and, in a vegetable garden, **cultivas** it. In autumn the leaves **se caen**.\n\nAn animal that may disappear **está en peligro de extinción**. To protect it there are **parques naturales**, where **está prohibido** cazar.\n\nComparing: **el** animal **más** grande **de** la tierra; **tan** rápido **como**; **más** peligroso **que**."
      }
    },
